## 5. AI model and hosting decisions

This was a major topic in the conversation.

### Your original model

You already have Gemma 3 4B installed through Ollama.

We established that you can use it for local development and testing without paying for inference. However, a model running on your laptop is not automatically available to users accessing a deployed website.

You also should not expose your local Ollama endpoint directly to the public internet.

### Your actual preference

You clarified that you are not committed to Gemma or to winning the Gemma-specific category. You are open to using another AI model if it is easier to host for free.

The goal is to select the model and hosting approach based on:

- Free or affordable online inference.
- Compatibility with Mastra.
- Reliable structured JSON output.
- Ability to extract transaction details correctly.
- Reasonable response speed.
- Suitable licensing and challenge eligibility.

### Models and services discussed

| Option                           | Role                     | Main consideration                                                                                                     |
| -------------------------------- | ------------------------ | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| Gemma 3 4B + Ollama              | Local development        | Already installed; free local inference, but not publicly hosted                                                       |
| Qwen2.5 1.5B Instruct            | Small open-weight model  | Can run locally with Ollama; public use still requires hosted inference or a server                                    |
| Cloudflare Workers AI            | Hosted inference service | A possible way to access eligible open-weight models using a free daily allocation, subject to quotas and availability |
| Hugging Face Inference Endpoints | Managed model hosting    | Infrastructure is managed for you, but running an endpoint may cost money                                              |
| RunPod                           | Cloud GPU infrastructure | Can host a model, but is generally a paid option                                                                       |

Earlier in the discussion, Cloudflare Workers AI was identified as having a documented free allocation of 10,000 Neurons per day at the time of the cited information. You would need to verify current quotas, eligible models and costs before choosing it.

Qwen2.5 1.5B Instruct was also considered as a lightweight alternative, but using it locally does not solve online hosting by itself.

### The recommended direction so far

Use Mastra with a suitable hosted open-weight model, potentially through Cloudflare Workers AI, instead of paying to maintain a dedicated model server.

This remains a proposed direction, not a final model/provider selection. The exact model and inference service have not yet been settled or tested.

You can continue using Gemma locally for comparison and development if useful, but you do not need to build the project around it.

