## 7. Financial correctness and security requirements

These were included in the project prompt and are important design constraints.

- Use deterministic application code for all money calculations.
- Validate AI output against a defined schema.
- Never save AI-extracted transactions without user confirmation.
- Ask for clarification when amounts or descriptions are ambiguous.
- Keep API keys, database credentials and model-provider secrets in environment variables.
- Never expose secrets in frontend code or commit them to Git.
- Isolate each user's business records so one user cannot access another's data.
- Add appropriate authentication before making private financial records available online.
- Clearly label net operating result; do not confuse it with a cash balance.
- Avoid claiming Ledger provides professional accounting, tax, investment or financial advice.
- Avoid sending unnecessary sensitive financial information to the model provider.

